abstract: >-
  Accountability infrastructure for AI agents: human-approved
  committed identities, least-privilege capability leases (scoped,
  limited, expiring, revocable), a fail-closed enforcement gate that
  ledgers every action attempt, a hash-chained ledger storing
  payloads as hashes, and an external replay audit that re-evaluates
  every allowed action against the lease terms. Generalized from
  identity-runtime into framework-agnostic infrastructure.
